WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:06.600
From tropical islands to dystopian wastelands&nbsp;
to the farthest reaches of the universe, here's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:12.840
where you've seen the cast members of Amazon's&nbsp;
music mockumentary Daisy Jones &amp; the Six before.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.620
Daisy Jones lead Riley Keough&nbsp;
has music in her blood. She's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.200
the granddaughter of King of&nbsp;
Rock 'n' Roll Elvis Presley,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.120
as well as the daughter of Lisa Marie Presley and&nbsp;
Danny Keough, both musicians in their own right.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:29.220
Riley Keough is also no stranger to musical&nbsp;
dramas, as her first on-screen role was the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:34.800
2010 biopic The Runaways, in which she played&nbsp;
Marie Currie. More big-screen features followed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:38.160
including Mad Max: Fury Road,&nbsp;
the crime caper Logan Lucky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:42.840
the psychological horror flick The&nbsp;
Lodge, and the A24 black comedy Zola.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:48.420
As for TV, in 2016 Keough was the lead on&nbsp;
Season 1 of the Starz anthology drama The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:52.260
Girlfriend Experience, an adaptation&nbsp;
of the 2009 Steven Soderbergh drama&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.600
starring former adult film star Sasha Grey.&nbsp;
Keough took another leading TV role in 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:01.140
this time on the Amazon&nbsp;
thriller The Terminal List.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:05.580
The band at the center of Daisy Jones&nbsp;
and the Six is led by Billy Dunne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.440
who's played by English actor Sam Claflin. He's&nbsp;
probably best known for his turns as Finnick in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:15.060
The Hunger Games series. He previously made his&nbsp;
big screen debut back in 2011 as Philip Swift,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:19.920
the young missionary captured by Blackbeard in&nbsp;
Pirates of the Caribbean: On Stranger Tides.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.780
Sticking with the franchise work, Claflin also&nbsp;
played William in Snow White and the Huntsman and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:29.820
its sequel. His other notable cinematic credits&nbsp;
include the survival drama Adrift, and the romance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:35.280
flicks Me Before You and Love Wedding Repeat. More&nbsp;
recently, he starred in Netflix's Enola Holmes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:39.180
in which he assumed the iconic role&nbsp;
of Mycroft, the eldest Holmes sibling.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:44.880
And over on the small screen, from 2019 to&nbsp;
2022, Claflin was a regular cast member on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.918
the British crime drama Peaky Blinders as&nbsp;
real-life politician Sir Oswald Mosley.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:54.817
"We deal in reasoned&nbsp;
principle, argument, and fact."

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:59.220
Former model Camila Morrone stars&nbsp;
on Daisy Jones as Camila Dunne,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:03.480
wife of bandleader Billy. If you know her&nbsp;
name but not her work, it's probably because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:09.000
of her controversial relationship with Leonardo&nbsp;
DiCaprio, which ended shortly after she turned 25.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:14.460
Morrone hasn't starred in anything huge yet, but&nbsp;
she has shown up in a few notable movies. In 2018,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.460 --> 00:02:18.900
she was one of the leads in the indie stoner&nbsp;
comedy Never Goin' Back, and she played the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:23.580
daughter of Bruce Willis' vigilante character&nbsp;
in the remake of Death Wish. And in 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:28.260
she showed up in Valley Girl, a remake of&nbsp;
the 1983 Nicolas Cage film of the same name.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:33.000
With a leading role on Daisy Jones, Morrone is&nbsp;
putting her modeling work behind her, as she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.620
focuses instead on her budding Hollywood career.&nbsp;
As she told The Wall Street Journal in 2020,

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:41.997
"I think it's hard for the world and also&nbsp;
the industry to be able to see you as both."

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:47.700
Model turned actress Suki Waterhouse stars in&nbsp;
Daisy Jones and the Six as keyboardist Karen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:52.020
a headstrong musician determined to break&nbsp;
the mold of women in show business. She's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:55.920
yet to have a true breakout role, but she&nbsp;
has appeared in plenty of notable films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:00.600
including the 2014 romantic dramedy&nbsp;
Love, Rosie, which also featured Sam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:05.280
Claflin. She also played Kitty Bennet in&nbsp;
2016's Pride and Prejudice and Zombies.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:09.780
Waterhouse finally secured a leading role in&nbsp;
the The Bad Batch, in which she fought off a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:15.360
gang of deranged cannibals in a dystopian future.&nbsp;
And then in 2019, she could be seen in Detective&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:21.960
Pikachu as Ms. Norman, the genetically modified&nbsp;
Ditto, and in the 2021 indie horror flick Seance.

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:26.040
"It's been a long time in the making, so we're,&nbsp;
we're, I think we're ready at this point."

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:30.480
While several actors from Daisy Jones&nbsp;
started out as models, Nabiyah Be's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:34.920
first career makes her even more suited for&nbsp;
a musical drama. She stars as Simone Jackson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:39.240
best friend to Daisy Jones. Though Be's&nbsp;
career in Hollywood has barely begun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:43.800
it's her life as a singer, songwriter, and&nbsp;
Broadway actress that proves her bona fides

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:48.300
Be has thus far appeared in just one feature&nbsp;
film, but it's one of the biggest of all time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:53.820
as she had a small role in 2018's superhero&nbsp;
epic Black Panther. She played Linda Johnson,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:58.140
a highly-trained black ops soldier and&nbsp;
girlfriend of the villainous Erik Killmonger.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:02.640
Hailing from Brazil, Be has received accolades&nbsp;
for her stage work, including the Drama Desk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:07.560
Award for her performance in School Girls; or The&nbsp;
African Mean Girls Play. She also played the role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:12.480
of Eurydice in the Off-Broadway version of the&nbsp;
Tony-winning Broadway musical Hadestown. Daisy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:17.940
Jones is her first major TV role, as she plays&nbsp;
a disco star who mentors the title character.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:23.340
Among the relative newcomers of the Daisy Jones&nbsp;
cast is Will Harrison, an Ithaca native who spent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:28.080
most of his young adult life in Massachusetts&nbsp;
before attending Carnegie Mellon School of Drama.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:33.720
In 2019, at the age of 22, Harrison appeared&nbsp;
on an episode of the CBS political drama Madam&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:37.680
Secretary. A year later, he starred in&nbsp;
the indie drama This is a Film About My&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:41.700
Mother. On Daisy Jones, he plays Graham&nbsp;
Dunne, younger brother of Billy and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:46.260
group's lead guitarist and co-founder. It's&nbsp;
a larger and meatier role than Harrison has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:50.280
ever played thus far in his career. He stands&nbsp;
to gain serious attention from the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:55.637
as a strong performance could spotlight his talent&nbsp;
on a larger stage and result in his big break.

00:04:55.963 --> 00:04:58.297
"That's the story that I had heard."

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:03.420
Sebastian Chacon may have one of the biggest&nbsp;
bodies of work among the lesser-known Daisy Jones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:08.520
cast members, as he's shown up in some of today's&nbsp;
biggest TV hits. He started his Hollywood career&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:13.800
with a small part on an episode of Madam Secretary&nbsp;
before moving on to the USA techno-thriller Mr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:18.540
Robot. From there, he showed up for a single&nbsp;
episode on a bunch of other shows in a wide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:23.640
range of genres, including the Batman prequel&nbsp;
Gotham and CBS' Sherlock Holmes series Elementary.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:29.040
Chacon eventually began snagging recurring roles,&nbsp;
including two episodes of Pose, a three-story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:34.560
stint on Tales of the City, and finally the part&nbsp;
of Fly Rico on Penny Dreadful: City of Angels.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:39.660
And as for the big screen, he had a key role&nbsp;
in the 2022 indie thriller Emergency. Now that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:44.917
he's a series regular on a hotly anticipated&nbsp;
show, he can finally call himself a star.

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:49.800
In the role of guitarist Eddie Roundtree is&nbsp;
little-known British actor Josh Whitehouse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:54.360
who boasts a modest but impressive resume. If&nbsp;
you've seen him before, it was likely on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:59.520
BBC historical drama series Poldark, on which&nbsp;
he was a main cast member for Seasons 3 and 4.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:04.440
The 2020 remake of Valley Girl was a starring&nbsp;
vehicle for Whitehouse, as he played Randy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:09.120
the '80s punk rocker who becomes the object&nbsp;
of desire for a Los Angeles teenage girl.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:13.440
The previous year he starred opposite Vanessa&nbsp;
Hudgens in the Netflix holiday romance movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:18.557
The Knight Before Christmas, in which he played a&nbsp;
14th-century knight transported to the modern day.

00:06:18.919 --> 00:06:22.999
"Love is the first and foremost&nbsp;
of all knightly virtues."

00:06:22.999 --> 00:06:27.359
In addition to Daisy Jones, Whitehouse is&nbsp;
due to star in the upcoming The Happy Worker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.359 --> 00:06:31.077
as well as the animated film&nbsp;
Ozi: The Voice of the Forest.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:35.220
Tom Wright plays Teddy Price, the&nbsp;
producer at the record company who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:39.000
first brings Daisy Jones to the attention&nbsp;
of The Six and sticks by their side as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:42.540
they rise to the top of the charts.&nbsp;
A longtime veteran character actor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:45.900
Wright is the kind of face you know you've&nbsp;
seen but might have trouble placing.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:50.880
Starting his career out in the early '80s, it's&nbsp;
possible you know Wright as the titular hitchhiker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:55.500
on the Creepshow 2 segment "The Hitchhiker."&nbsp;
You may also recognize him from any number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.500 --> 00:07:00.120
of '80s and '90s favorites, as he racked up&nbsp;
credits in plenty of movies from those decades,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:04.440
including Tales From the Hood. As for TV,&nbsp;
Trekkies will no doubt remember him as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:07.800
ill-fated transporter creation that&nbsp;
was doomed to die on the Star Trek:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:12.300
Voyager episode "Tuvix." Meanwhile, sitcom&nbsp;
fans may remember him from four episodes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:17.280
of Seinfeld as Mr. Morgan, the skeptical&nbsp;
Yankee Stadium coworker of George Costanza.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:21.060
After appearances on a number of hit&nbsp;
dramas, Wright became a series regular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:26.640
on the BYUtv series Granite Flats, as&nbsp;
FBI agent Ezekiel Scott. More recently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:32.155
he starred on the 2020 Netflix sitcom Medical&nbsp;
Police, on which he played CDC Director Patten.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:37.800
There may be only one man more important to Daisy&nbsp;
Jones and the Six's success than producer Teddy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:43.080
Price, and that would be manager Rod Reyes.&nbsp;
He's played by the legendary Timothy Olyphant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:47.880
who's enjoyed a career bringing to life charming&nbsp;
rogues and swaggering do-gooders. He's something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:52.500
of a modern-day John Wayne, as he's best known&nbsp;
for playing a couple of iconic lawmen. First&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:57.240
there was US Marshal Seth Bullock on the&nbsp;
groundbreaking HBO Western Deadwood. That&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:01.500
led to his starring turn as Raylan Givens,&nbsp;
the sharp-shooting, steely-eyed gunslinging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:06.120
marshal on FX's crime drama Justified, which&nbsp;
is easily his most iconic work to date.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:12.240
Olyphant then showed off his funny side beginning&nbsp;
in 2017 on the Netflix zombie sitcom Santa Clarita&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:17.040
Diet alongside Drew Barrymore. Then he returned&nbsp;
to the role of a marshal on Season 4 of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:21.960
anthology series Fargo. After playing himself&nbsp;
on the sitcoms The Good Place and The Grinder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:25.860
he played a marshal once again, but&nbsp;
this time in a galaxy far, far away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:30.060
on the Star Wars Disney+ series The&nbsp;
Mandalorian and The Book of Boba Fett.

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:35.640
As for the movies, Olyphant's most notable roles&nbsp;
include James Stacy in 2019's Once Upon a Time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:42.240
in Hollywood and Mickey in Scream 2 all the way&nbsp;
back in 1997. And he's set to have a busy 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:47.697
as he's due to return to the role of Raylan Givens&nbsp;
for the miniseries Justified: City Primeval.

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:50.940
"You might want to factor them items into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:53.837
equation before you decide&nbsp;
what you gonna do next."

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:55.920
If you're a fan of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.920 --> 00:09:01.320
crime dramas, you no doubt know the name, or at&nbsp;
least the face, of Jacqueline Obradors. She has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:06.240
a recurring role on Daisy Jones as Lucia, but&nbsp;
for the past several decades she's been a small&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:11.040
screen stalwart, including on a couple of the&nbsp;
most well-regarded crime dramas of their day.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:16.200
From 2001 to 2005, Obradors played&nbsp;
Detective Rita Ortiz on NYPD Blue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:19.260
She appeared in 80 episodes of&nbsp;
the series, which led to guest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:23.820
appearances on plenty of other shows. She&nbsp;
eventually landed another regular role,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:28.680
this time as another detective on the Amazon crime&nbsp;
procedural Bosch, beginning with season five.

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:33.780
Though she's always been more of a TV actor,&nbsp;
Obradors does have a few notable movie roles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:39.300
on her resume. Fans of the 2001 animated Disney&nbsp;
sci-fi adventure Atlantis: The Lost Empire may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:44.280
recognize her as the voice of teenage mechanic&nbsp;
Audrey. She also appeared in the Wesley Snipes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:51.360
action thriller Unstoppable in 2004 and in 1998's&nbsp;
action-adventure comedy Six Days, Seven Nights.

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:55.920
Another relative newcomer to Hollywood,&nbsp;
Ayesha Harris plays Bernie on Daisy Jones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.920 --> 00:10:00.720
which is her biggest part to date. A barber in&nbsp;
her pre-acting days before she left Long Beach,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:04.440
California, Harris made her&nbsp;
on-screen debut in 2017,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:09.180
when she appeared on an episode of The CW&nbsp;
horror series Two Sentence Horror Stories.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:13.080
While Harris' role on Daisy Jones is a&nbsp;
potential turning point in her career,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:18.060
it's not as if she's never been on a hit series.&nbsp;
She's mostly had minor blink-and-you’ll-miss-'em&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:22.980
roles, but maybe in 2022 you noticed her when&nbsp;
she made a delivery on an episode of the ABC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:27.360
sitcom Abbott Elementary. She also made&nbsp;
her big screen debut that same year in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:31.980
anthology film Tell it Like a Woman, which was&nbsp;
nominated for Best Original Song at the Oscars.

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:36.780
2023 is shaping up to be an even bigger year&nbsp;
for Harris. In addition to playing Bernie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:39.240
she's also signed up for the&nbsp;
Netflix series Glamorous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:42.480
on which she'll appear alongside&nbsp;
Kim Cattrall in the story of a young&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:47.736
gender nonconforming queer person who gets&nbsp;
a gig working for a renowned makeup artist.

